WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.280
City is united as one! We're all friends!

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.540
The Friendship Cup enters its third day.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.260
We'll be starting the second round today.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.730
Here are the eight challengers 
that won in the first round!

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.160
Who will be the four to win their 
way to the pinnacle from here?

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.950
The first match of destiny is...

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:28.290
Yuzu Hiiragi versus Sergey Volkov!

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.280
Yuya knows what he needs to do.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.990
"To make the people smile,

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.560
I need to get the viewers to acknowledge me.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.690
To achieve that...

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:47.640
I have to beat Jack!"

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.730
Yuya wants to convince people that 
the Friendship Cup is wrong.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.170
I want make the Synchro Dimension's people

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.240
fear the interdimensional war, too.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.850
To do that, I must fight this duel 
with all I have and win.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.560
D-Wheels.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.770
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.450
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.880
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.020
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.960
The Beauty of Destruction

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.750
Listen to those cheers.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.520
Here they are.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:13.970
First, that cute, pretty entertainment angel, 
currently skyrocketing in popularity...

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.940
Yuzu Hiiragi, age 14!

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.920
She's looking even better than in the first round.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.360
You're so cute, Yuzu, dear!

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.620
I mean, Yuzu Hiiragi.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.590
Jack Atlas...

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.340
I need to keep moving toward him.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.890
That's the only way I can convey 
our feelings to everyone.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:44.040
That's why I need to give the 
current duel all I've got.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.610
Isn't that right, Yuya?

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:50.310
Yuzu, do your best.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:56.090
Here he is! Her opponent, Sergey!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.680
In his first-round match with Damon, 
he seemed unimpressive,

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.870
but he got a lucky win.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.920
Will he be better today?

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:08.630
He has none of the presence of the great criminal

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.770
that once had all City trembling.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.600
Go, Yuzu! Put the thumbscrews to him!

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.010
Yuzu Hiiragi...

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:25.980
She and Serena will make fine trump cards 
to use when erecting my kingdom.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.830
You must defeat her and bring her to me.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.650
Now, as you know,

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:37.260
the course was destroyed in yesterday's 
fight between Kurosaki and Dennis.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.620
Here, in the second round,

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:42.590
we'll be holding the riding duels 
outside the Duel Palace!

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.520
Now, Action Field, on! Crossover Acceleration!

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.520
Duel mode, on. Autopilot, stand by.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.260
Riding duel...

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.340
Acceleration!

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:19.450
Duel!

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:27.110
In this duel, whoever passes first through 
the Duel Palace's gate gets the first turn.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:29.070
Yuzu rockets out ahead!

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:30.500
Yes!

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.810
This is the first tournament to 
use the duel lanes outside.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.050
Who will take the first turn?

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:42.650
You can expect a more dynamic, 
speedy, and hardcore duel!

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.620
I'm counting on you two!

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:49.350
The Tops do enjoy their spectacle.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.330
I'm sure they'll be quite satisfied.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.740
Sergey just sped up.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.300
He's pulled up next to Yuzu!

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.600
Now, which will reach the gate first?

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.850
Yuzu gets the first turn!

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.220
Watch me, Yuya.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:16.320
I summon Canon the Melodious 
Diva from my hand!

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.090
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:30.010
Summoning Canon prepares my 
side of the field for the next turn.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.200
Now, bring it on!

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:35.670
My turn.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.980
I summon Thorn Prisoner Van.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.850
0 attack points?

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:49.040
I-Incredible, Sergey summoned 
a 0-attack-point monster,

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.570
in attack, not defense, position?

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.730
Shouldn't you summon it in defense 
position, with 0 attack points?

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:58.460
I end my turn.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.370
A 0-attack-point monster in attack position?

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:06.870
Intentional?

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.660
What is he thinking?

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.540
Wondering won't get me anywhere.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.050
My turn!

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:18.180
I activate my trap card Melodious Rhythm Change!

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.880
I return one Melodious monster 
on the field to my hand,

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.990
to Special Summon another Melodious 
monster from my hand!

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:32.070
I Special Summon Mozarta the Melodious Maestra!

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.800
I activate Mozarta's effect!

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:41.440
Once per turn, I can Special Summon one 
Melodious monster, Level 4 or below.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:45.850
Return, Canon the Melodious Diva!

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.080
This is boring.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:53.490
I also summon Solo the Melodious 
Songstress from my hand!

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.400
A third one?

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:06.000
In a flash, Yuzu has added three 
monsters to the field!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.450
And Sergey's monster has 0 attack points.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.970
Is it over already?

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.840
Great! Finish him off!

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:17.210
Battle!

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:20.680
I attack Van with Mozarta!

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.400
Sergey took 2600 points of damage!

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.170
I activate Van's effect.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.520
When this card is attacked,

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.440
I can show one Thorn Prisoner card in my hand,

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:38.840
and pay 400 life points of damage 
to reduce battle damage to 0.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:43.300
I have, in my hand, Thorn Prisoner Darli.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:54.910
Sergey took 400 damage to avoid 2600!

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.310
And the destroyed Van's effect

00:08:58.310 --> 00:09:03.760
allows me to Special Summon 
it with Thorn Prisoner Darli.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:15.800
Another monster with 0 attack points?

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:20.040
Sergey's summoned both in attack position...

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.380
What is he thinking?

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:28.380
I attack Darli with Solo the Melodious Songstress!

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:31.180
I activate Darli's effect.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:34.320
If, on my opponent's Battle Phase,

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.660
a Thorn Prisoner is on my field besides Darli,

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:41.460
I can pay 400 life points to negate the attack.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.430
I still have an attack left!

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.720
I attack Darli with Canon!

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.980
Darli can't use its effect again! Go, Yuzu!

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.960
Will Sergey use an Action Card to dodge?

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:19.270
Just as Canon attacks, Sergey...

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.700
Sergey accidentally took big damage.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.800
How embarrassing, after showing off like that!

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:38.900
Are you all right?

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:40.780
You're hurt!

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:44.860
I now end my turn!

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.330
Beautiful...

00:10:55.080 --> 00:11:00.890
My, my. Roget's supposed right hand 
seems to be having a hard time.

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:05.680
He's...

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.370
Here they come!

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:13.520
My turn.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:18.020
I summon a second Thorn Prisoner 
Darli from my hand.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:27.130
Level 1 Darli tunes Level 1 Van.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.720
Tear open the warped appetites of the flesh.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.940
And submit, body and soul, to the thorns.

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:35.210
Synchro Summon.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:41.320
Come forth, Level 2 Thorn Observer Zuma.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.160
Zuma's effect activates.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:50.860
When this card is successfully Synchro Summoned,

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:55.500
all monsters on the field gain one thorn counter.

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:05.700
Monsters with thorn counters cannot attack.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.760
And during our turn's End Phase, 
we each take 400 damage

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:17.420
for each thorn counter on 
our monsters on the field.

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:21.420
I set one card and end my turn.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:27.090
At the same time, I take 400 
damage from Zuma's effect.

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:35.880
Sergey tied up all the monsters

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:38.740
and chipped away at his life 
to keep them from attacking.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:43.110
A bad sign... I certainly hope nothing happens.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:49.680
Yuzu's monsters on the field have 
had their attacks sealed.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.600
How will she fight?!

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.580
It isn't over yet. I'm just getting started!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.470
I'll put everything I have into this draw.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:56.970
My turn!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.360
I got it... Polymerization!

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:05.830
I activate my Continuous Trap Thorn Growth.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:10.570
Its effect doubles the damage 
dealt by thorn counters!

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:22.510
Due to Zuma, I'll take 2400 damage during 
my End Phase if I don't do something.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:25.450
But now, I'll show my stuff.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:28.620
I activate my spell card Polymerization!

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:34.890
I fuse Mozarta, Canon, and Solo.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:40.390
The supreme genius, the triumphant 
chorus, the angel's song...

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:43.230
Follow the baton and stack your power!

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:45.210
Fusion Summon!

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.600
Now come to the stage, to sing 
the song of passion!

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:52.630
Bloom Prima the Melodious Choir!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.220
For each of its fusion components,

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:59.700
Bloom Prima's attack points increase by 300.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.540
Bloom Prima has three fusion components!

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.930
I activate the effect of Thorn Growth.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.780
When thorn counters leave the field,

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:14.890
I take 100 points of damage for each.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.490
What's with that guy?

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:23.980
He actually seems happy about losing life...

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:28.440
Battle. I attack Zuma with Bloom Prima!

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:33.100
I activate Zuma's effect.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.790
When this card is attacked

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.990
and its synchro components are in my graveyard,

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:42.230
I pay 400 life to reduce battle damage to 0.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:47.610
And Zuma's leaving the field means

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:53.470
I take 100 points of damage 
from Thorn Growth's effect!

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:03.080
When there are no thorn counters 
on the field, this card is destroyed.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:07.240
And Zuma's effect lets me Special Summon

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.220
the Zuma sent to the graveyard and 
its Synchro-component monsters.

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:20.460
The monster that was just destroyed 
returns with its two components!

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:24.570
And all three have 0 attack points, but are 
summoned in attack position!

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:28.280
What is this? Is this his strategy?

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:29.870
I'm not done yet.

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:34.150
Bloom Prima can attack twice 
during one Battle Phase.

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:36.510
I attack Zuma again!

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:39.580
I activate Darli's effect.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:42.350
When you declare battle, just once,

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:45.790
if there is another Thorn Prisoner 
monster on the field,

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:49.590
I can pay 400 life to negate the attack.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.600
Sergey negated the other attack.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:58.240
But his own card's effect chipped away 
at his life, leaving him only 200!

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.970
It's almost like he's trying to self-destruct.

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:03.880
What's he plotting?

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:07.560
It seems it's over.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.450
Before a volcano erupts,

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.100
it stores magma to the bursting point.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:17.520
As if it's burning itself with incandescent heat,

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.500
preparing to thrust the pain into the sky.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:25.640
I end my turn.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.390
Sergey has 200 life.

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:31.600
I can win on my next turn.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:33.540
But any more of this...

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.380
Hey!

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:40.410
It's dangerous to continue this duel further!

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:42.880
He's hurt!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:47.160
Okay, but the match isn't over yet.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:49.950
You really need to see it through to the end...

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.550
Yeah! Yeah!

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:52.860
See it through!

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.830
Finish him off already!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:59.640
It's wrong to force a man 
on his last legs to duel.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.340
You're looking forward to seeing someone 
sent underground that much?

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:07.540
I'm like Yuya.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:12.240
I think the way the Friendship Cup 
does things is wrong!

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:13.980
Yuzu...

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:18.650
If you keep this up, your hearts 
will never truly be united.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:22.820
You won't be able to resist 
Academia's coming invasion!

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:29.290
Right now, what you really need 
is to bring your hearts together!

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:35.170
Build true friendships, and stand against 
Academia and the interdimensional war!

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:39.400
Yeah... When you win a duel, 
that's when they listen to you.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.630
Everyone, listen!

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:42.700
You...

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:47.340
You think you've already won?

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:51.690
Not that you're going to win... 
But that you already have?

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:53.510
That's what you seem to think.

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:59.980
It isn't a face of one desperately trying to 
win, but one already sure of victory...

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:02.560
That is most beautiful when crushed.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.020
Beautiful?

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:07.530
Endure, endure, endure...

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:11.500
Endure, endure... It was worth the endurance!

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:15.350
I endured, I endured, I endured, 
I endured, I endured...

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.980
I endured it all!

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:24.280
So much for the limiter, eh?

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:29.150
It seems he'll need more work.

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:32.840
That Damon fellow I fought in the first round...

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.130
He just wouldn't do.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:38.840
That duel wasn't beautiful at all!

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:41.280
But you're different.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.870
You cared that I was injured, and you 
were sure that you'd won.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:46.880
It's beautiful...

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:49.320
A truly beautiful battle.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:52.120
Now, let's give it a beautiful finish.

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:54.640
With your loss!

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:01.750
My turn! I activate my spell card Polymerization!

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:02.950
Polymerization?

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:07.400
This card's effect fuses Van, Darli, and Zuma.

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:11.160
Toil! Pain! Murder mediocrity,

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.700
strip everything away, and pass 
along the road of thorns

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.170
Fusion Summon!

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:24.110
Appear, Thorn Overserver Vandarlizuma!

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:32.820
A-After all that, he's summoned another 
0-attack-point monster in attack position!

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:38.350
I'm not sure he's even trying to 
stay in the fight, let alone win!

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:39.580
There's a trick to it.

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:41.030
Yuzu, be careful.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.490
My loss?

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:47.970
What will he do with 0 attack points?

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:50.810
Vandarlizuma's attack points

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:55.970
become double the difference between 
2500 and my life points!

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:59.580
Sergey has 200 life...

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:00.950
Which means...

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:03.680
4600 attack points!

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:08.150
And once per turn, I can pay 100 life

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:13.020
to reduce one of your monster's 
attack points to 100...

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:16.500
Until your turn's End Phase!

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:22.090
Vandarlizuma's attack points increase even more!

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:25.640
4800 attack points?

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:29.570
Sergey comes on so strong, it's like his 
previous indifference didn't exist!

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:34.350
For the sake of this effect, he shaved 
away his own life points?

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.820
Take a glancing blow, to score a decisive one.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:40.660
No, it's more than that.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:45.690
Vandarlizuma attacks Bloom Prima!

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.470
An Action Card!

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:02.620
Your struggle is beautiful.

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:03.310
But...

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:07.710
Unsightly!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:15.960
Yuzu!

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:20.300
Lone flower that bloomed on the battlefield,

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.660
scatter!

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:43.350
Beautiful...

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:46.060
Fool!

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.790
All available security to the place she landed.

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:52.430
That's a surprise!

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:56.260
Sergey achieves an unbelievable 
come-from-behind victory!

00:21:56.770 --> 00:22:00.400
While Yuzu Hiiragi appears to have 
been thrown from the duel lane,

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:02.730
crashing into a nearby building.

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:06.990
Smoke is rising from the building, 
and we can't see inside.

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:10.790
We can't tell if Yuzu is safe or not!

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:13.400
Yuzu!

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:52.780
Yuzu... Is Yuzu safe?!

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:55.450
No one cares what happens to the losers.

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.750
When a piece is off the board, it's gone.

00:23:58.030 --> 00:23:58.870
Gone?

00:23:59.530 --> 00:24:01.130
No one will save her?

00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:02.650
Losers are abandoned.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:05.180
That's how things work in this world.

00:24:05.180 --> 00:24:07.290
That's what we're fighting for...

00:24:07.290 --> 00:24:09.560
To overturn this rotten world!

00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:13.160
If you want to say something, say it after you win!

00:24:13.160 --> 00:24:16.650
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Storm of Revolution.

00:24:16.650 --> 00:24:18.540
The fun is only getting started!
